IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sga-time`
IMPORT `sga-seat`

-- sga-cases-seat.l4: worked cases for the seat layer, one or more for each question, in the order of sga-seat.l4.
-- Expected values are hand-written from the text of the Act (compilation C2026C00272, plain-text conversion), not copied from any run.
-- The running scenario: an employer pays an employee qualifying earnings on Wednesday 1 July 2026 (the QE day).
-- The usual period then ends on the seventh business day after the QE day, Friday 10 July 2026, if there are no public holidays;
-- the extended usual period ends on the 20th business day after it, Wednesday 29 July 2026.
-- The charge percentage is 12, so a payment of qualifying earnings of $5,000 gives an individual superannuation guarantee amount of $600.

§ `Part 2: who is my employee`

-- Ordinary meaning only: an employee.
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- None of the facts the section mentions, and not an employee in the ordinary meaning: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Works under a contract wholly or principally for their labour (s 12(3)): an employee.
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A member of the Parliament of a State (s 12(5)): an employee.
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paid to do domestic work for not more than 30 hours a week (s 12(11)): not regarded as an employee in relation to that work.
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A member of a local government council (s 12(9A)) is not an employee of the council, unless covered by paragraph 12-45(1)(e) (s 12(10)).
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I treat this person as my employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Part 3: the amount I must contribute (ss 10A, 15A to 17D)`

-- 10A(5): a cap of $30,000 over a charge percentage of 12 is $250,000 exactly; a cap of $27,500 gives $229,166.67, rounded down to the nearest $10.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum contributions base for the year` 30000 EQUALS 250000
#ASSERT `What is the maximum contributions base for the year` 27500 EQUALS 229160
-- 10A(6): the employee has been paid $248,000 this financial year and the base is $250,000: a payment of $4,000 counts only up to the base ($2,000); a payment after the base is reached counts as nil.
#ASSERT `How much of my payment counts as qualifying earnings` 248000 4000 250000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `How much of my payment counts as qualifying earnings` 250000 1000 250000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of my payment counts as qualifying earnings` 0 4000 250000 EQUALS 4000
-- 17A(2): two payments on the QE day of $4,000 and $1,000: $5,000 at 12% is $600.
#ASSERT `What is my individual superannuation guarantee amount` 0 250000 (LIST 4000, 1000) FALSE EQUALS JUST 600
-- Already $248,000 earlier in the year: only $2,000 counts in all, so $240.
#ASSERT `What is my individual superannuation guarantee amount` 248000 250000 (LIST 4000, 1000) FALSE EQUALS JUST 240
-- 17B: nil if an exemption certificate covers the employer and employee for the QE day.
#ASSERT `What is my individual superannuation guarantee amount` 0 250000 (LIST 4000, 1000) TRUE EQUALS JUST 0
-- No payment on the QE day: the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `What is my individual superannuation guarantee amount` 0 250000 EMPTY FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 17D: a certificate for the period 1 April to 30 September 2026 covers 1 July 2026 but not 1 October 2026.
#ASSERT `Does my certificate cover the QE day` (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my certificate cover the QE day` (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) (Date 1 10 2026))

§ `Part 3: which contributions count, and the base shortfall (ss 18A to 18C)`

-- Arguments: sacrificed; to a complying fund; able to be allocated in the fund; for a defined benefit member; conversion notice in effect; to an RSA; able to be allocated in the RSA; the employee has died and the equivalent is paid; notional; written statement obtained; 18B(2) applies.
-- A contribution to a complying fund that can be allocated for the employee: eligible.
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, but a sacrificed contribution: not covered by paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same, but for a defined benefit member: not eligible under paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A written statement is conclusively presumed to show a complying fund, but not the other elements (18A(2), Note 1).
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The presumption is unavailable if section 18B(2) applies on the day.
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A contribution to an RSA that can be allocated: eligible; one that cannot: not.
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An amount paid to the legal personal representative of a deceased employee (18A(1)(c)); a notional contribution to a defined benefit scheme (18A(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my contribution count as an eligible contribution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Arguments for the next three questions: the QE day; the public holidays; item 1 applies; the first standard QE day after the QE day; the day a determination was made; the latest due day.
-- No holidays, no table item: the usual period ends on the seventh business day, Friday 10 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must a contribution be received to count` (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS Date 10 7 2026
-- A holiday on Friday 3 July 2026 pushes the seventh business day to Monday 13 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must a contribution be received to count` (Date 1 7 2026) (LIST (Date 3 7 2026)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS Date 13 7 2026
-- Item 1: the extended usual period ends on the 20th business day, Wednesday 29 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must a contribution be received to count` (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS Date 29 7 2026
-- Item 2: the usual period for the first standard QE day, 15 July 2026, ends on Friday 24 July 2026.
#ASSERT `By what day must a contribution be received to count` (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE (JUST (Date 15 7 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS Date 24 7 2026
-- Item 3: 20 business days starting the day after a determination made on 15 July 2026 end on Wednesday 12 August 2026, later than 29 July.
#ASSERT `By what day must a contribution be received to count` (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 7 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS Date 12 8 2026
-- Item 4: a latest due day of 20 July 2026 is later than the end of the usual period.
#ASSERT `By what day must a contribution be received to count` (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (Date 20 7 2026)) EQUALS Date 20 7 2026
-- Received on 8 and 10 July 2026: in time. Received on 11 July 2026: not in time, unless item 1 applies. Received on 15 January 2026: within the 12 months before the QE day.
#ASSERT `Was my contribution received in time to count` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 8 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was my contribution received in time to count` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 10 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was my contribution received in time to count` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 11 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was my contribution received in time to count` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 14 7 2026) EMPTY TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was my contribution received in time to count` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 15 1 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Base shortfall: the amount is $600; $400 received on 8 July 2026 counts; $100 received on 14 July 2026 does not (after 10 July): $200.
#ASSERT `What is my individual base shortfall` 600 (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST 400, 100) (LIST (Date 8 7 2026), (Date 14 7 2026)) EQUALS JUST 200
-- With item 1, 14 July 2026 is in time too: $100.
#ASSERT `What is my individual base shortfall` 600 (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST 400, 100) (LIST (Date 8 7 2026), (Date 14 7 2026)) EQUALS JUST 100
-- $700 received in time exceeds the amount: no shortfall, and not less than nil.
#ASSERT `What is my individual base shortfall` 600 (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING (LIST 700) (LIST (Date 8 7 2026)) EQUALS JUST 0
-- No contributions: the whole $600.
#ASSERT `What is my individual base shortfall` 600 (Date 1 7 2026) EMPTY FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY EMPTY EQUALS JUST 600

§ `Part 3: the final shortfall, notional earnings and the uplift (ss 18D, 19A, 19B)`

-- The late period runs from the day after 10 July to the day before the assessment (section 6(1)): with an assessment on 20 July 2026, 11 to 19 July is 9 days; with an assessment on 13 July 2026, 11 and 12 July is 2 days.
#ASSERT `How many days are in my late period` (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `How many days are in my late period` (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 13 7 2026) EQUALS 2
-- Final shortfall: $200 base; $100 received 14 July 2026 is within the late period (11 to 19 July); $50 received 21 July 2026 (after the assessment on 20 July) is not.
#ASSERT `What is my individual final shortfall` 200 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) (LIST 100, 50) (LIST (Date 14 7 2026), (Date 21 7 2026)) EQUALS 100
-- If both were received by the assessment day: nil, and not less than nil.
#ASSERT `What is my individual final shortfall` 200 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) (LIST 100, 150) (LIST (Date 14 7 2026), (Date 15 7 2026)) EQUALS 0
-- Notional earnings: $200 base, a late period of two days (an assessment on 13 July 2026) at 1% a day, compounded daily: $2.00 then $2.02, $4.02.
#ASSERT `What is my individual notional earnings component` 200 100 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 13 7 2026) (LIST 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS JUST 4.02
-- A final shortfall of nil: no days are counted.
#ASSERT `What is my individual notional earnings component` 200 0 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 13 7 2026) (LIST 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS JUST 0
-- Two days but three daily rates given: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `What is my individual notional earnings component` 200 100 (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 13 7 2026) (LIST 0.01, 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Uplift: 60% of ($500 + $100) is $360; less a reduction of $60 under the regulations is $300; a reduction larger than the amount leaves nil.
#ASSERT `What is my administrative uplift amount` 500 100 0 EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `What is my administrative uplift amount` 500 100 60 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `What is my administrative uplift amount` 500 100 400 EQUALS 0

§ `Part 3: the choice loading and the total shortfall (ss 16B, 20 to 20D)`

-- Arguments: Subdivision E applies; section 20A(2) or (3) applies; the contributions it applies to; the other eligible contributions within the notice period.
-- 25% of $2,000 is $500, under the $1,200 limit.
#ASSERT `What is my choice loading` TRUE TRUE 2000 0 EQUALS JUST 500
-- 25% of $6,000 is $1,500, capped at the $1,200 limit.
#ASSERT `What is my choice loading` TRUE TRUE 6000 0 EQUALS JUST 1200
-- Other contributions of $1,000 earlier in the notice period reduce the limit by $250 to $950.
#ASSERT `What is my choice loading` TRUE TRUE 6000 1000 EQUALS JUST 950
#ASSERT `What is my choice loading` TRUE TRUE 2000 1000 EQUALS JUST 500
-- 20A(2) and (3) do not apply: a loading of nil. Subdivision E does not apply: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `What is my choice loading` TRUE FALSE 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `What is my choice loading` FALSE TRUE 2000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 16B(2): final shortfalls $100 + $50, notional earnings $4 + $2, uplift $90, choice loading $500: $746.
#ASSERT `What is my superannuation guarantee shortfall` (LIST 200, 300) (LIST 500) (LIST 100, 50) (LIST 4, 2) 90 EQUALS JUST 746
-- No base shortfall and no choice loading greater than nil: section 16B does not apply.
#ASSERT `What is my superannuation guarantee shortfall` (LIST 0, 0) (LIST 0) (LIST 0, 0) (LIST 0, 0) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 30: an arrangement made to avoid the charge; the Commissioner thinks $1,000 would have been payable.
#ASSERT `How much charge am I liable to pay under section 30` TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `How much charge am I liable to pay under section 30` TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part 3A: the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C to 32ZAB)`

-- Chosen fund (32C(1)); arguments: chosen fund; unfunded public sector scheme; Commonwealth employee in the CSS or PSS; direct cost imposed.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the chosen fund compliant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 32CA: a direct cost or charge on the employee makes it not comply.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the chosen fund compliant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unfunded public sector scheme counts unless the employee is in the CSS or PSS.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the chosen fund compliant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the chosen fund compliant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the chosen fund compliant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Stapled fund (32C(1A), (1B)); arguments: no chosen fund; notification names the stapled fund; required to give a form; not given in time; direct cost.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the stapled fund compliant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the stapled fund compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the stapled fund compliant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the stapled fund compliant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Fund named on the standard choice form (32C(2), (2A), (2AA)); arguments: no chosen fund; no stapled fund; eligible choice fund; specified in the form; temporary visa; MySuper; MySuper death benefit; other death benefit; required to give form; not given in time; direct cost.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the fund I named compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A temporary visa holder: paragraph (2)(ba) does not apply, so the fund need not be specified in the form.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the fund I named compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the fund I named compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the fund I named compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the fund I named compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Successor fund (32C(2AB)); arguments: transferred without consent; the original fund was one to which the earlier paragraphs applied; successor fund; direct cost.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the successor fund compliant` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution to the successor fund compliant` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Industrial instruments (32C(6), (6AAA)); arguments: under one of the listed agreements or awards; under a determination or enterprise agreement before 1 January 2021; notification of no stapled fund; direct cost.
#ASSERT `Is my contribution under an industrial instrument compliant` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution under an industrial instrument compliant` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution under an industrial instrument compliant` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my contribution under an industrial instrument compliant` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Standard choice form (32N, 32NA). Arguments: a trigger occurred; then the eleven exceptions in the order of section 32NA.
#ASSERT `Must I give this employee a standard choice form` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I give this employee a standard choice form` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I give this employee a standard choice form` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No trigger and no exception: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Must I give this employee a standard choice form` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A form for an employee employed on 1 July 2005 is due before 29 July 2005.
#ASSERT `Did I give the standard choice form in time` `the employee was employed by the employer on 1 July 2005` (Date 1 7 2005) (Date 28 7 2005) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I give the standard choice form in time` `the employee was employed by the employer on 1 July 2005` (Date 1 7 2005) (Date 29 7 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A form for a new employee who started on 1 July 2026 is due within 28 days: 28 July is within on either way of counting; 30 July is not; 29 July depends on the way of counting.
#ASSERT `Did I give the standard choice form in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 28 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did I give the standard choice form in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did I give the standard choice form in time` `the employee first commenced employment with the employer` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 32P: a form is a standard choice form if it is in writing, has the three statements, and (for a defined benefits scheme member) the scheme information.
#ASSERT `Is my form a standard choice form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my form a standard choice form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my form a standard choice form` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my form a standard choice form` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my form a standard choice form` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- 32F(2): a notice given on 15 July 2026 makes the fund the chosen fund 2 months later, on 15 September 2026, or an earlier day the employer sets after the notice.
#ASSERT `From what day is the chosen fund the chosen fund` (Date 15 7 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT `From what day is the chosen fund the chosen fund` (Date 15 7 2026) (JUST (Date 1 8 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2026)

§ `Part 4: statements and assessments (ss 33, 36, 37)`

-- 33(2): lodged on 19 July 2026 before an assessment on 20 July 2026, in the approved form: a voluntary disclosure statement; lodged on the day of the assessment: not.
#ASSERT `Is my statement a voluntary disclosure statement` (Date 19 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my statement a voluntary disclosure statement` (Date 20 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my statement a voluntary disclosure statement` (Date 19 7 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) FALSE)
-- 36(3): a payment day of Friday 3 July 2026 gives the seventh business day after, Tuesday 14 July 2026; a holiday on Monday 6 July 2026 gives Wednesday 15 July 2026.
#ASSERT `What receipt day is taken` (Date 3 7 2026) EMPTY EQUALS Date 14 7 2026
#ASSERT `What receipt day is taken` (Date 3 7 2026) (LIST (Date 6 7 2026)) EQUALS Date 15 7 2026
-- 37(2): no avoidance: the subsection does not apply. Fraud or evasion: at any time. Otherwise within 4 years from the day the assessment was made (1 July 2026).
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 7 2030) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 7 2040) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment` TRUE FALSE (Date 29 6 2030) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Commissioner still amend my assessment` TRUE FALSE (Date 2 7 2030) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Part 6: unpaid charge (s 49)`

-- Due on 29 July 2026 and unpaid at the end of 31 July 2026: three days, $10 + $11 + $12 = $33. Too few daily amounts for the days: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `How much general interest charge do I owe` (Date 29 7 2026) (Date 31 7 2026) (LIST 10, 11, 12) EQUALS JUST 33
#ASSERT `How much general interest charge do I owe` (Date 29 7 2026) (Date 31 7 2026) (LIST 10, 11) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Part 7: the notice to pay and the administrative penalty (ss 59A to 59E)`

-- 59A: charge imposed on 1 July 2026: the 28-day period starting that day ends on 28 July 2026, and the trigger day is 29 July 2026.
#ASSERT `On what day does the notice trigger day fall` (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS Date 29 7 2026
-- A notice must be given if some of the amount is the 59A(1) amount, the rest is unpaid charge, the amount exceeds $30, there was no earlier notice in the 50 days before the trigger day, and no part was in an earlier notice.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 100 NOTHING NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 30 NOTHING NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The 50 days ending 28 July 2026 start on 9 June 2026: an earlier notice on 9 June blocks it; one on 8 June does not.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 100 NOTHING (JUST (Date 9 6 2026)) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 100 NOTHING (JUST (Date 8 6 2026)) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A higher prescribed amount of $200: $200 does not exceed it, $201 does.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 200 (JUST 200) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 201 (JUST 200) NOTHING TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner give me a notice to pay` (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE TRUE 100 NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A notice specifying 29 July 2026: the payment period ends on the 28th day after, 26 August 2026.
#ASSERT `On what day does the payment period end` (Date 29 7 2026) EQUALS Date 26 8 2026
-- 59C: arguments: imposition day; day specified in the notice; first and last days an 18C(4) determination covers the employer; days of earlier penalties greater than nil; the amount unpaid at the end of the payment period.
-- Item 3: 25% of $1,000 is $250.
#ASSERT `What penalty will I owe` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) NOTHING NOTHING EMPTY 1000 EQUALS JUST 250
-- Item 2: an earlier penalty on 1 September 2025 is within the 24 months ending 27 August 2026: 50% of $1,000 is $500.
#ASSERT `What penalty will I owe` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (LIST (Date 1 9 2025)) 1000 EQUALS JUST 500
-- An earlier penalty on 27 August 2024 is outside those 24 months (they start 28 August 2024): 25%.
#ASSERT `What penalty will I owe` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) NOTHING NOTHING (LIST (Date 27 8 2024)) 1000 EQUALS JUST 250
-- Item 1: a determination covering the employer from 1 June 2026 with no end: 0%, whatever earlier penalties there were.
#ASSERT `What penalty will I owe` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) NOTHING (LIST (Date 1 9 2025)) 1000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- A determination that ended on 30 June 2026, before the imposition day, does not reach the period: item 3 applies.
#ASSERT `What penalty will I owe` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) (JUST (Date 30 6 2026)) EMPTY 1000 EQUALS JUST 250
-- 59D(3): notice given on 1 September 2026: a due day of 15 September 2026 is 14 days after; 14 September is not.
#ASSERT `Is my penalty due at least 14 days after the notice` (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 15 9 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my penalty due at least 14 days after the notice` (Date 1 9 2026) (Date 14 9 2026))

§ `Part 8: payments to employees (ss 63A to 71)`

#ASSERT `Is my payment one to which Part 8 applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my payment one to which Part 8 applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my payment one to which Part 8 applies` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my payment one to which Part 8 applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Part 9: the amnesty and records (ss 74, 79)`

-- Arguments: the day the Royal Assent was received (15 January 2021, made up: the amnesty period then ends 15 July 2021); the day of the disclosure; approved form; relates to the shortfall; not disclosed before; the last day of the quarter; the Commissioner had said it was looking into compliance.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for the amnesty` (Date 15 1 2021) (Date 1 7 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2018) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A quarter ending 30 June 2018: its 28 days end on 28 July 2018, after the amnesty period started on 24 May 2018.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for the amnesty` (Date 15 1 2021) (Date 1 7 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 30 6 2018) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Disclosed after the amnesty period ended; not in the approved form; the Commissioner had already said so.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for the amnesty` (Date 15 1 2021) (Date 16 7 2021) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2018) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for the amnesty` (Date 15 1 2021) (Date 1 7 2020) FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2018) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for the amnesty` (Date 15 1 2021) (Date 1 7 2020) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2018) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- With an assent day of 31 August 2020 the period ends on "31 February 2021": a disclosure on 1 March 2021 is on the day the text does not settle.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for the amnesty` (Date 31 8 2020) (Date 1 3 2021) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 31 3 2018) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 74(2): a shortfall of $500 with the information and none without it: $500; $200 without it: only the increase, $300.
#ASSERT `For how much of my shortfall do I qualify for the amnesty` 500 0 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `For how much of my shortfall do I qualify for the amnesty` 500 200 EQUALS 300
-- 79(1) to (3): all four requirements met; any one missing.
#ASSERT `Am I keeping the records the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I keeping the records the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I keeping the records the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- 79(4): records prepared on 1 July 2026 and the acts completed on 1 January 2027 must be kept until the end of 5 years after the later, about 1 January 2032.
#ASSERT `Must I still keep these records` (Date 15 3 2030) (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I still keep these records` (Date 15 3 2032) (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 79(5): not required if the Commissioner has said so, or the company has been finally dissolved.
#ASSERT `Must I still keep these records` (Date 15 3 2030) (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I still keep these records` (Date 15 3 2030) (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
